OL,3,GNEWSAThe boxing club helping veterans
OL,4,Arebuild lives
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Ian Dewey left the Army after more
OL,7,Fthan 13 years of service, he struggled
OL,8,Fto adjust to civilian life.
OL,10,FThe 47-year-old veteran had served in
OL,11,FNorthern Ireland, Iraq and Bosnia and
OL,12,FHerzegovina, but said life outside the
OL,13,Fforces felt unfamiliar and isolating.
OL,15,F"I left the forces and didn't know what
OL,16,Fit was, but [I found] people a bit
OL,17,Fslow," he said.
OL,19,F"They could not get things done quick
OL,20,Fenough, with the speed and accuracy of
OL,21,Fwhat we were like in the army."
